Subject: [PATCH sdk1-0003] Give sdk_core's static library a fixed target name

sdk_core/CMakeLists.txt names its library `${PROJECT_NAME}_static`, and
sdk_core itself never calls project(). Standalone that yields the accidental
`Project_static` (CMake invents `project(Project)` and warns — see
spikes/s8-mid70-sdk1/build-fix/cmake.log and its libProject_static.a). Added
as a subdirectory of the engine, PROJECT_NAME is *scanengine*, so the SDK
would define a target called `scanengine_static` — a name that reads as ours,
that collides with anything the engine ever adds under that name, and that
would silently change if the engine project were renamed.

Pinning it to `livox_sdk_static` mirrors SDK2, whose sdk_core sets
`livox_lidar_sdk_static` literally, and gives engine/CMakeLists.txt a stable
name to link. One line, and it is the smallest change that makes the
subdirectory build well-defined; the alternative (wrapping the add_subdirectory
in a project() call of our own) would put the SDK in its own project scope and
drag CMAKE_* settings out of sync with the engine's.
---
--- a/sdk_core/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/sdk_core/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.10)
 
-set(SDK_LIBRARY ${PROJECT_NAME}_static)
+set(SDK_LIBRARY livox_sdk_static)
 add_library(${SDK_LIBRARY} STATIC "")
 
 set(LIVOX_SDK_MAJOR_VERSION "2")
